    <string name="step_no_root">Allow SoundPower in Magisk\'s Superuser list, then try again.</string>
    <string name="step_no_magisk">SoundPower is installed with a Magisk module, and needs Magisk 24.0 or newer.</string>
    <string name="step_install">Install the SoundPower module. It patches the audio effects configuration systemlessly; uninstalling it in Magisk undoes everything.</string>
    <string name="step_update">Update the module to the version that matches this app.</string>
    <string name="step_reboot">Reboot to load the module.</string>
    <string name="step_disabled">The module is disabled. If audio crashed during boot, the module\'s watchdog disabled it: see log/boot.log in the module directory before enabling it again.</string>
    <string name="step_not_loaded">The module is installed, but the audio service has not loaded the effect. Reboot if you just installed or enabled it; otherwise see diag.txt in the module directory.</string>
    <string name="step_incompatible">The effect and this app speak different protocol versions. Install the module that comes with this app.</string>
    <string name="step_ready">Everything is in place.</string>

